---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { legal } from '../data/legal';
import { path } from '../data/site';
---
<LegalLayout slug="privacy" eyebrow="Your information" title="Privacy policy" updated={legal.privacyUpdated} description="How Form + Field collects, uses, and protects the personal information of clients and website visitors.">
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>This website does not set cookies, run analytics, or load advertising or social-media trackers. We collect only what is needed to schedule and deliver your sessions, we never sell personal information, and you can ask us to correct or delete your information at any time.</p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>{legal.tradeName} is operated by {legal.legalName}, {legal.entityType}, based in Larkspur, {legal.state}. We provide private Pilates instruction, equine bodywork, and Horse + Rider sessions. For privacy questions, use the contact details at the bottom of this page.</p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p><strong>When you browse this website:</strong> the site is a set of static pages. Our hosting provider records standard server logs (your IP address, browser type, the pages requested, and the time of the request) to operate and secure the service. We do not add tracking of our own and we do not have access to individual visitors' identities from these logs.</p>
  <p><strong>When you book or contact us:</strong> we collect the information you provide, such as your name, email address, phone number, appointment details, and any notes you share about your goals, movement history, injuries, or your horse. If you book online, this information is entered into Square, our scheduling and payment provider, and is subject to Square's privacy policy as well as this one.</p>
  <p><strong>Payment information:</strong> we never see or store your full card number. Payments are processed by Square, which handles card data under its own security and PCI obligations.</p>
  <p><strong>Health and injury information:</strong> anything you tell us about your body, injuries, medical conditions, or your horse's condition is used only to plan and adapt your sessions safely. We are not a medical or veterinary provider and this information is not protected health information under HIPAA, but we treat it as confidential and share it with no one without your permission, unless required by law.</p>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To schedule, confirm, remind you about, and deliver your appointments.</li>
    <li>To process payments and keep the records that tax and accounting rules require.</li>
    <li>To adapt sessions to your goals, experience, and any limitations you tell us about.</li>
    <li>To respond to your questions and requests.</li>
    <li>To comply with legal obligations and protect the safety of clients, horses, and the studio.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not use your information for advertising, we do not send marketing emails unless you have asked for them, and we do not build profiles or make automated decisions about you.</p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We share personal information only with service providers that help us run the business, and only for the purposes described here:</p>
  <ul>{legal.processors.map(p => <li><strong>{p.name}</strong>: {p.purpose}. <a class="inline-link" href={p.policy} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Privacy policy</a>.</li>)}</ul>
  <p>We may also disclose information if required by law, to enforce our <a class="inline-link" href={path('terms')}>Terms of service</a>, or to protect someone's safety. We do not sell personal information and we do not share it with data brokers or advertisers.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>Booking and payment records are kept for as long as you are a client and for the period required by tax and accounting rules (generally seven years), after which they are deleted or anonymized. Session notes are kept while you are an active client and deleted on request. Server logs are retained by our hosting provider according to its own retention schedule.</p>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask us at any time to see the personal information we hold about you, correct it, or delete it, and you can withdraw consent to any optional use. Contact us using the details below and we will respond within 30 days. Deleting information may mean we can no longer provide sessions or keep records the law requires us to keep; we will tell you if that applies.</p>
  <p>If you are a Colorado resident, the Colorado Privacy Act gives certain rights against businesses that process large volumes of personal data. We currently fall well below its thresholds, but we honor the same principles: access, correction, deletion, and no sale of your data.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This website is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone under 13 online. Clients under 18 may attend sessions only with a parent or legal guardian's written consent, and we collect that guardian's contact information rather than the minor's.</p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>This website is served over HTTPS and stores no client data itself. Booking and payment data are held by Square, which uses industry-standard encryption. We limit access to client information to the people who need it to deliver your sessions.</p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>Booking links take you to Square's website. Once there, Square's privacy policy applies. We are not responsible for the privacy practices of other websites.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>When we make material changes we will update the date at the top of this page. Continued use of our services after a change means you accept the updated policy.</p>
</LegalLayout>
